    alt='Paper 1, Figure 1. Five-stage pipeline: exteroceptive and interoceptive prediction errors are precision-weighted, the somatic marker scales interoceptive precision only, the weighted errors accumulate as S_t, and ignition with global broadcast follows when S_t exceeds θ_t.',
    caption=['APGI architecture: a five-stage pipeline in which modality-specific prediction errors are precision-weighted, the somatic marker M̂(c,a) amplifies interoceptive precision only, the weighted errors accumulate as S_{t}, and frontoparietal–thalamic workspace neurons broadcast once S_{t} exceeds the allostatically regulated threshold θ_{t}.'],
