fig(section=P1, id='P1F2', heading='Figure 2. Somatic-marker disinhibition circuit', image='P1F2.png', width=6.5,
    alt='Paper 1, Figure 2. (A) vmPFC drives VIP+ interneurons that inhibit SST+ Martinotti cells and release the L2/3 pyramidal dendrite. (B) At baseline SST+ inhibition is intact; on somatic-marker retrieval it is weakened and interoceptive precision rises. (C) An L5 pyramidal cell with a dendritic calcium plateau triggered by apical–basal coincidence.',
    caption=['Proposed somatic-marker disinhibition circuit. (A) vmPFC retrieval of the somatic-marker value M̂(c,a) drives VIP^{+} interneurons in anterior insula, which inhibit SST^{+} Martinotti cells and release the L2/3 pyramidal dendritic compartment. (B) At M̂(c,a) ≈ 0, SST^{+} inhibition of the dendrite is intact; at high M̂(c,a), VIP^{+} suppression of SST^{+} disinhibits the dendrite and raises effective interoceptive precision Π^{i}_{eff} ahead of ignition. (C) In L5 thick-tufted pyramidal cells, coincident apical and basal input triggers a dendritic Ca^{2+} plateau and somatic burst firing (Larkum et al., 1999); APGI proposes that this burst channel carries precision-weighted interoceptive error.'],
    source=['Type: anatomical/mechanistic schematic (proposed circuit). Implements Π^{i}_{eff} = Π^{i}_{baseline}·exp(β_{SM}·M̂(c,a)). Evidence tier: Plausible (correlational anatomical support); causal validation requires optogenetic or chemogenetic dissociation. No statistics.'])

fig(section=P1, id='P1F3', heading='Figure 3. Thermodynamic bridge and the κ parameter', image='P1F3.png', width=6.5,
    alt='Paper 1, Figure 3. Derivation chain from ATP per spike to about 0.12 J per ignition event, the separate uncalibrated bridge parameter κ in ATP per bit, and the whole-event Landauer erasure ratio R_L of about 10^18, shown as non-interconvertible quantities.',
    caption=['The thermodynamic bridge and the κ parameter. Schematic of the metabolic cost of conscious access, tracing ATP per spike through spikes per ignition event to ~2.4 × 10^{18} ATP ≈ 0.12 J per event (§4.6, Appendix E). The schematic holds two quantities apart. The bridge parameter κ converts Tier-2 ignition-event information into Tier-1 energy and is uncalibrated: sensitivity calculations span ~3 × 10^{3} to ~10^{9} ATP/bit across bit-count conventions, and no value is adopted. The erasure ratio ~{R}_{L} refers the whole-event energy to the Landauer floor for the ~13–27 bits discarded at accumulator reset, giving ~10^{18}. A per-bit unit cost and a whole-event ratio are not interconvertible; keeping them apart is what this figure exists to do.'],
    source=['Type: derivation schematic. No empirical calorimetry performed; the event-energy chain is an independent accounting, not a measurement. **Key quantities.** Landauer minimum k_{B}·T·ln 2 = 2.97 × 10^{−21} J/bit at 310 K. ATP hydrolysis free energy 5.07 × 10^{−20} J (ΔG°′ 30.5 kJ/mol; standard-state value — the in vivo |ΔG| of ≈ 50–60 kJ/mol would raise joule figures ≈ 1.7–2-fold without changing κ in ATP units). Event energy ≈ 2.4 × 10^{18} ATP ≈ 0.12 J per ignition event (spike-count accounting); the independent BOLD-calibrated estimate is ≈ 2 × 10^{18} ATP ≈ 0.10 J. Erased-state count N_{erase} ≈ log_{2}(S/δ_{S}) ≈ 13–27 bits for δ_{S} = 10^{−4}–10^{−8}. Erasure ratio ~{R}_{L} ≈ 1–3 × 10^{18}.',
            '**κ status.** Uncalibrated; no value adopted. Sensitivity calculations span ~3 × 10^{3} to ~10^{9} ATP/bit depending on the bit-count convention (Paper 1, §4.6). Calibration requires a matched same-network, same-window measurement of event energy against event information. Registered bands: consistent [10, 10^{3}]; requires explanation (10^{3}, 10^{4}]; bridge-inconsistent outside [10, 10^{4}], where the per-bit bridge is retired if the out-of-band value replicates after matched calibration. No current sensitivity value lies inside the consistent band: the synaptic-storage convention (3.4 × 10^{3}) falls in the requires-explanation band, every other value exceeds 10^{4}, and the direct per-bit estimates of Laughlin et al. (1998) lie at or above its upper edge. No Landauer multiple is reported for κ, which counts broadcast rather than erased information.',
            '**Overhead factors** — distinct referents, never interchangeable. Whole-event erasure ratio ~{R}_{L} ≈ 1–3 × 10^{18}, the event energy referred to the N_{erase} Landauer floor; this is the only Landauer quantity in the strict sense. Per-operation bound ≈ 4 × 10^{12}, the event energy referred to ~10^{7} irreversible synaptic operations. Scene-content bound ≈ 4 × 10^{13}, the event energy referred to ~10^{6} scene-content bits. See Paper 4, Table 2 (register of record).'],
    comments=[('Laughlin et al. (1998) lie at or above', 'Confirm the position of the Laughlin et al. (1998) per-bit estimates relative to 10^4 against Paper 1, §4.6, before submission.')])

